From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paolo Pisati <paolo.pisati@canonical.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 10:40:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] UBUNTU: SAUCE: apparmor: fix unterminated prompt string in
 Kconfig

The prompt of SECURITY_APPARMOR_PACKET_MEDIATION_ENABLED is missing its
closing quote, so every Kconfig run warns:

  security/apparmor/Kconfig:132:warning: multi-line strings not supported

Kconfig ends the string at the newline, so the symbol still works, but
the warning is emitted once per architecture on every config update.
Close the string and fix the "defauit" typo while at it.

Fixes: 8a52d43f9774 ("UBUNTU: SAUCE: apparmor5.1.0 [24/25]: apparmor: skb: add the ability to use interface in network mediation.")
Signed-off-by: Paolo Pisati <paolo.pisati@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00246
Ledger-Origin: ubuntu@d98c34180be1898b17a9fc022a2983e0268940df
---
 security/apparmor/Kconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/security/apparmor/Kconfig b/security/apparmor/Kconfig
index fc0bb4955820..d57c301d64db 100644
--- a/security/apparmor/Kconfig
+++ b/security/apparmor/Kconfig
@@ -129,7 +129,7 @@ config SECURITY_APPARMOR_RESTRICT_USERNS
 	  by their profile.
 
 config SECURITY_APPARMOR_PACKET_MEDIATION_ENABLED
-	bool "Enable AppArmor packet mediation by defauit
+	bool "Enable AppArmor packet mediation by default"
 	depends on SECURITY_APPARMOR && NETWORK_SECMARK
 	default n
 	help
